### Open follow-ups

- aide_brain remediation text for no-mcp-entry/mcp-drift (and the aide_info description) tells the user to run `npx … sync` themselves. This conflicts with the brain.md anti-pattern. It is pre-existing and not fixed in this cycle.
- The work-kanban guide is ~990 lines, read in full on every /kanban call. Consider splitting it into an index plus a file per operation.
- The installAgents spec claims the kanban skill outcome, but installSkills stages it (scope attribution).
- brain.md Step 3's malformed branch wording fits syntax faults better than read errors.

## Process discipline (permanent)

- One implementor per numbered plan step.
- .claude/ files are edited directly, never pipelined.
- Pause for user approval before the build.

